  "name": "A Systematization of Security Vulnerabilities in Computer Use Agents",
  "notes": "Reviewed against the complete retained original arXiv abstract. Experimental results and artifact availability have not been independently reproduced. This is a threat analysis with case studies; the annotation does not imply a standardized public benchmark or independently validated defenses.",
  "published_at": "2025-07-07",
  "relations": [],
  "review_status": "curated",
  "scope": "core",
  "summary": "Analyzes security boundaries in computer-use agents through a risk taxonomy and concrete adversarial case studies. It links observed failures to input provenance, interface-action binding, memory, and delegation, and proposes CUA-specific evaluation principles.",
